<%- layout('./layout/boilerplate.ejs') %>

<header class="soon-header">
  <a class="soon-mark" href="/">Curate</a>
  <div class="soon-header-actions">
    <span class="soon-status">Coming soon</span>
    <button id="theme-toggle" class="btn btn-sm" aria-label="Toggle theme" title="Toggle dark/light mode">
      <i class="fas fa-moon"></i>
    </button>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="soon">
  <div class="soon-intro">
    <h1>A library for the links you keep opening.</h1>
    <p>
      Curate is a browser extension for developers. You save docs, repos, tools, and articles from a popup in your toolbar, then find them again without digging through a bookmarks bar.
    </p>
    <p>
      The extension is not public yet. Chrome and Edge builds are on the way.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="soon-body">
    <section id="about">
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>
        Most bookmarking tools either dump everything into one list or try to be a social product. Curate is smaller than that. It is a private library that lives next to the page you are already on.
      </p>
      <p>
        You sign in inside the popup, save a link with a title, category, and tags, and optionally file it into a collection. Later you open the same popup and go back to that link, or to a whole set of related ones.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="features">
      <h2>What it will include</h2>

      <div class="soon-feature">
        <h3>Bookmarks</h3>
        <p>Save a title, URL, category, and tags from the popup. Open the link later in one click. Edit or delete it without leaving the extension.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="soon-feature">
        <h3>Collections</h3>
        <p>Group related bookmarks into named sets, such as a stack you are learning or a project you are shipping. Open a collection to see only those links, and add new ones straight into it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="soon-feature">
        <h3>Accounts in the popup</h3>
        <p>Create an account or sign in from the extension. Edit your profile, change your password, log out, or delete your account there. The website is not the place you manage your library.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="soon-feature">
        <h3>Private by default</h3>
        <p>Links and notes stay on your account. There is no public feed, no sharing wall, and no one else browsing your library.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="soon-feature">
        <h3>Light and dark</h3>
        <p>A readable popup in both modes, so it works at a desk or late at night without becoming a different product.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="soon-feature">
        <h3>Library first</h3>
        <p>The home screen is your collections and bookmarks. Forms stay out of the way until you add or edit something.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="soon" class="soon-close">
      <h2>Coming soon</h2>
      <p>
        Curate will ship as a Chrome and Edge extension. There is no download and no web signup on this site yet. Check back here when it is ready.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>
